---
title: Overview
description: How a contract is built from the services picked on an opportunity, approved, signed, filed and delivered.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Contracts are prepared on an opportunity in CRM. The person in charge picks the services on the opportunity, and Operon builds the contract from the firm's template: the scope and fee sections list exactly the services picked, at the agreed prices. A discounted contract goes to the department lead for approval. The firm always signs with its signatory's saved signature; the client signs online or on paper. Every file of the deal stays with the opportunity, and once the client pays, the signed services open their cases.

## The stages of a contract

| Stage | What happens |
|---|---|
| **1 Prepare** | Choose the client, the client signatory, the issuing entity, the language and the format. |
| **2 Draft** | Read the generated contract through; edit the wording if needed. |
| **3 Approval** | Only when needed: a discount above the firm's threshold, or a draft edited by hand. |
| **4 Signing** | Send for e-signature, or record a copy signed on paper. |
| **5 Signed** | The signed copy is filed with the opportunity. The services can be invoiced and delivered. |

## Who does what

| Role | Work |
|---|---|
| **Department lead** | Keeps the department's services, packages, prices, payment terms and contract wording up to date. Approves discounted contracts. |
| **Person in charge (PIC)** | Picks the services and prices on the opportunity, prepares and generates the contract, submits it and sends it for signing. |
| **Director in charge** | Signs contracts for the firm. The firm's signature on a contract is always the saved signature of the opportunity's Director in charge. |
| **Tenant admin** | Maintains the contract settings, the issuing entities, the contract signatories with their saved signatures, and the contract templates. Approves a contract that a department lead submitted. |

